WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.475
OT telemetry is the foundation of visibility into industrial systems.

00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:09.725
It includes network communication, process values, device and controller events, endpoint logs,

00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:12.787
alarms, identities, remote sessions, and configuration changes.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:16.725
Each source answers different questions and carries different limitations.

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:18.474
Useful telemetry combines layers.

00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:21.537
Network data shows paths and protocol behavior.

00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:25.037
Process data shows physical conditions and control response.

00:00:25.037 --> 00:00:29.849
Endpoint and system logs identify users, files, services, and local changes.

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:32.037
Protocol context explains industrial operations,

00:00:32.037 --> 00:00:35.974
while asset and maintenance context explains why they matter.

00:00:35.974 --> 00:00:37.724
Safe collection is essential.

00:00:37.724 --> 00:00:42.536
Passive observation and existing logs are often preferred near sensitive systems,

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:47.786
and any new agent, query, or configuration should be tested with engineering.

00:00:47.786 --> 00:00:51.724
Visibility must not undermine reliability, availability, or process integrity.

00:00:51.724 --> 00:00:55.661
Quality requires completeness, accuracy, synchronized time, useful retention, normalization,

00:00:55.661 --> 00:00:57.848
asset mapping, and honest coverage.

00:00:57.848 --> 00:01:02.223
Blind spots and noisy data should be measured and managed.

00:01:02.223 --> 00:01:07.911
Collection alone is not success if teams cannot trust or interpret the result.

00:01:07.911 --> 00:01:12.723
Security operations use telemetry for detection, hunting, incident response, anomaly analysis,

00:01:12.723 --> 00:01:14.473
inventory, and vulnerability prioritization.

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:18.848
The strongest programs connect those workflows with operators and engineers,

00:01:18.848 --> 00:01:24.098
turn findings into improvements, and continually align evidence with the real architecture.

00:01:24.098 --> 00:01:27.160
OT telemetry does not replace operational judgment;

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.660
it gives that judgment a stronger factual foundation.
